  "goodToKnow": "Glimpflich means lightly or without serious harm, almost always with verbs of outcome: glimpflich ausgehen, ablaufen, davonkommen (to get off lightly). News reports often say Der Unfall ging glimpflich aus. A similar idiom is mit einem blauen Auge davonkommen (to escape with a black eye). The word comes from old Glimpf (leniency)."
